Determination||Poem.text:
Emancipation fades away,
As the road of hope falls astray;
The future is barricaded all the way,
The waves of freedom kept at bay,
And my mind is elusive through the day,
And evasive through the night;
But it remembers my cold hands, cuffed tight,
While innocence was out of sight,
Hidden by the creepy absence of light;
But I’ll stand up and fight to make things right!

Nomad||Poem.text:
The man of no tenure,
The man of no culture,
Who sporadically wanders around;
He cannot endure,
His blurry life has no cure;
Where can his soul be found?
